Reports from customers across the U.S. and Japan continue to surface in our forums and on social media platforms, so be sure to keep an eye on your pre-order. Apple has a history of underpromising and overdelivering with delivery dates for new products, so shipping estimates starting to improve is not too surprising.<br/>
<br/>
iPhone Duo pre-orders <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/16/iphone-duo-now-available-to-pre-order/">began on Friday</a>, with shipping estimates on Apple's online store for newly-placed orders getting <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/16/iphone-duo-preorder-shipping-wait-times/">pushed back to January 25</a> within the first 30 minutes of pre-orders starting. In a statement issued later on Friday, Apple said demand for the iPhone Duo was "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/16/apple-iphone-duo-demand-extraordinary/">nothing short of extraordinary</a>."<br/>
